Patch 22: disable extended partitions at speed 1, on 1080p and below only.

Standalone. The conservative reading of patch 0019's split result -- included as
the floor of this round rather than its ambition.

0019 cleared the bar on A2 (1080p) at ratio 37.9 with +22.75% speedup, and
missed on A1 (4K) at 30.6. Both-classes-must-pass disqualified it. This patch
scopes the feature to the class where it already qualifies, banking the measured
1080p win and leaving 4K exactly as it is.

+22.75% is the second-largest single speedup measured anywhere in this project,
behind only the CCSO early-termination promotion. Declining to ship it because
it also fails on a class it can simply be scoped away from would be leaving a
large, verified gain on the table for no benefit.

Patches 20 and 21 attempt the harder thing -- making the feature qualify at 4K
too, by gating on pyramid level and by splitting the extended-partition family
respectively. If either succeeds it supersedes this patch and should be
preferred, since a feature that works at both resolutions is worth more than one
scoped to half the test set. This patch is what to land if both fail.

Resolution-conditioned speed features are idiomatic in this file --
is_480p_or_larger and is_720p_or_larger already gate several assignments -- so
this introduces no new kind of dependency, only a new instance of an existing
one.

The 2560 threshold puts 1080p and below inside the feature and 4K outside it.
-DAVM_S1_EXT_PART_MAX_WIDTH=0 disables the promotion entirely; raising the value
widens the scope back toward 0019.

diff --git a/av2/encoder/speed_features.c b/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
index f363519..4e8a265 100644
--- a/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
+++ b/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
@@ -349,6 +349,34 @@ static void set_good_speed_features_framesize_independent(
     sf->inter_sf.skip_compound_prune_top_refs_num_ref0 = 1;
     sf->inter_sf.skip_compound_prune_top_refs_num_ref1 = 2;
     sf->inter_sf.reduce_comp_refs = 2;
+    // Disable extended partitions at speed 1 on 1080p and below only.
+    //
+    // This is the conservative reading of patch 0019's split result. It cleared
+    // the bar on A2 (1080p) at ratio 37.9 with +22.75% speedup and missed on A1
+    // (4K) at 30.6. Rather than trying to recover A1, this scopes the feature to
+    // the class where it already qualifies, banking a large measured win at
+    // 1080p and leaving 4K untouched.
+    //
+    // It is included as the floor of this round, not its ambition. Patches 20
+    // and 21 attempt to make the feature work at 4K as well, and if either
+    // succeeds it supersedes this. If both fail, this still ships +22.75% on
+    // 1080p, which is the second-largest single speedup measured anywhere in
+    // this project.
+    //
+    // Resolution-conditioned speed features are idiomatic in this file --
+    // is_480p_or_larger and is_720p_or_larger already gate several -- so this
+    // introduces no new kind of dependency.
+    //
+    // -DAVM_S1_EXT_PART_MAX_WIDTH=0 disables the promotion entirely.
+#ifndef AVM_S1_EXT_PART_MAX_WIDTH
+#define AVM_S1_EXT_PART_MAX_WIDTH 2560
+#endif
+#if AVM_S1_EXT_PART_MAX_WIDTH
+    if (cm->width < AVM_S1_EXT_PART_MAX_WIDTH) {
+      sf->part_sf.disable_ext_partitions = true;
+    }
+#endif
+
     sf->inter_sf.disable_switchable_refinemv = 1;
     sf->inter_sf.prune_refinemv_by_ref_idx = 1;
     sf->inter_sf.prune_interintra_by_ref_idx = 1;
